# =============================================================================
# tun2socks source pin — SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH for the wrapper image build.
#
# Consumed by:  fetch-tun2socks.sh (build stage of ../Dockerfile)
# Mirrored by:  TUN2SOCKS_PIN in apps/api/src/services/redroid-service.js
#               (guarded in sync by tests/unit/redroid-t2s-pin.test.js)
#
# Rules:
#  - VERSION is pinned; the asset URL is DERIVED (v<VERSION>/<ASSET>) — a
#    floating 'latest' is structurally impossible and the fetch script
#    refuses any URL containing 'latest'.
#  - SHA256 is of the INNER binary (tun2socks-linux-amd64), not the zip.
#  - MIT-licensed upstream (xjasonlyu/tun2socks). Static x86-64 ELF → runs
#    in the redroid Android x86_64 userspace on an x86_64 host kernel.
#
# Verified 2026-10-20 (R1): zip downloaded from the pinned URL, inner
# sha256 = 98d545a6…c031, ELF 64-bit x86-64 static stripped, `--version`
# = tun2socks-2.7.0 (evidence: docs/runbook.md §10.1 / R1 progress log).
# =============================================================================
# NOTE: each assignment is of the form VAR=${VAR:-default} — a pre-set
# environment variable WINS (the fetch script documents these as TEST KNOBS;
# production callers pass no env and get the pinned defaults).
TUN2SOCKS_VERSION=${TUN2SOCKS_VERSION:-2.7.0}
TUN2SOCKS_ASSET=${TUN2SOCKS_ASSET:-tun2socks-linux-amd64.zip}
TUN2SOCKS_INNER_FILE=${TUN2SOCKS_INNER_FILE:-tun2socks-linux-amd64}
TUN2SOCKS_SHA256=${TUN2SOCKS_SHA256:-98d545a663b790b4a4100d0c796e1d43d82c5442efdb6e9c4d82e2e32e99c031}
